# The committed version recipe, sourced by lib/common.sh. To bump: edit here, or let renovate do it
# (renovate.json5 customManagers). A merged bump pushes to main, which is what triggers a rebuild.
#
# Both pins feed the build fingerprint, so changing either one produces a new `<upstream>-<revision>` release
# and changing neither produces nothing. See docs in README.md.

## The upstream release whose linux-<arch> binary we package. Its tag is also OUR version prefix.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=prometheus-community/smartctl_exporter
SMARTCTL_EXPORTER_VERSION="v0.14.0"

## Base image, digest-pinned. It supplies the smartctl binary the exporter shells out to, so a base bump is a
## real change to what we ship, not just a rebuild.
# renovate: datasource=docker
ALPINE_IMAGE="alpine:3.24@sha256:28bd5fe8b56d1bd048e5babf5b10710ebe0bae67db86916198a6eec434943f8b"
